$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 355-42-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A Typical Procedure for Triphasic U-tube
Chlorination of Benzyl alcohol 1a using SOCl2 (Table 2, entry 1). A
solution of 1a (54 mg, 0.5 mmol) and 1-hydroxybezotriazole (200 mg,
1.5mmol) in dichloromethane (1 ml) was put into one side of the u-tube,
in which FC-72 (3 ml) was placed and SOCl2 (0.15 mL, 2 mmol) was put into
the other side of the U-tube. The reaction progress was monitored by GC
analysis. Benzyl alcohol 1a was consumed for 4 h. The dichloromethane
layer was decanted and poured into water. The mixture was extracted with
ether, washed with a saturated NaCl aqueous solution, and concentrated.
The residue was purified by short column chromatography on silica gel
with hexane. To give benzyl chloride 3a in 95% yield (60 mg, 0.47
mmol)time 4 h.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fluorous Solvent as a New Phase-Screen Medium between Reagents and
Reactants in the Bromination and Chlorination of Alcohols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nakamura, Hiroyuki; Usui, Taikou; Kuroda, Hirokazu; Ryu, Ilhyong;
Matsubara, Hiroshi; Yasuda, Shinji; Curran, Dennis P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2003), 5(8), 1167-1169

