$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedures for the Halogenation of Benzyl alcohols
2-(3-Methoxyphenyl)benzyl chloride. To a solution of
2-(4-methoxyphenyl)benzyl alcohol (85.6 mg, 0.4 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL)
was added Et3N (0.082 mL, 0.6 mmol) and methanesulfonyl chloride (0.038
mL, 0.48 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at room
temperature, concentrated in vacuo, and then purified by a silica gel
column chromatography (EtOAc/n-hexane, 1:4) to afford the desired product
(100 mg, 99%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.55-7.53 (m, 1H), 7.39-7.31 (m,
4H), 7.01 (m, 2H), 6.98-6.93 (m, 1H), 4.54 (s, 2H), 3.84 (s, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.3, 141.9, 141.4, 134.8, 130.5, 130.1, 129.3,
128.4, 127.9, 121.5, 114.4, 113.3, 55.2, 44.4; IR (Film) ν 3063, 3002,
2834, 1653, 1540, 1419, 1320, 1222, 1022, 995, 757, 670 cm-1; HRMS (EI+)
m/z calcd. for C13H13ClO [M]+: 232.0655, found: 232.0655.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly efficient and versatile synthesis of polyarylfluorenes via
Pd-catalyzed C-H bond activation
