$DATUM 67-68-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of Benzyl Alcohols: Benzyl
Chloride (Table 1, Entry 1); Typical Procedure. The procedure for the
chlorination of benzyl alcohol (Table 1, entry 1) is representative for
all benzyl alcohols in Table 1. To a soln of benzyl alcohol (519 mg, 4.81
mmol) in anhyd DMSO (5 mL) was added TCT (487 mg, 2.64 mmol) portionwise.
The mixture was stirred at r.t. and the reaction was monitored by TLC
until completion (30 min). Then, the mixture was added to Et2O (50 mL),
and the organic phase was washed with H2O (5 × 30 mL), dried over anhyd
Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure to give the crude product
which was then filtered through a silica gel pad with petroleum ether to
afford benzyl chloride. Table 1, Entry 14: Yield 99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly chemoselective and rapid chlorination of benzyl alcohols under
neutral conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sun, Lili; Peng, Guisheng; Niu, Hongmei; Wang, Qiang; Li, Chunbao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2008), (24), 3919-3924

