$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4'-Chloromethyl-biphenyl-2-yl)-4,4-dimethyl-4,5-dihydrooxazole (10)
Thionyl chloride was added (2.0 g, 0.017 mol) dropwise to a solution of
[2'-(4,4-dimethyl-4,5-dihydro-oxazol-2-yl)-biphenyl-4-yl]-methanol 9 (4.0
g, 0.014 mol) in methylene chloride (40.0mL) at 0-5°C, and the
temperature was maintained for 2 h. The reaction mixture was poured into
an aqueous solution of 20% of sodium hydrogen carbonate solution (40.0
mL). The organic layer was separated and washed twice with water (50.0
mL). The organic layer was reduced under pressure to give the title
compound 10 as a white solid (4.2 g, 99% yield).
2-(4'-Chloromethyl-biphenyl-2-yl)-4,4-dimethyl-4,5-dihydrooxazole (10),
yield 4.2 g, 99%. melting point: 73-75°C; IR (cm-1) 1620 (C=N); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) (δ ppm) 7.73 (ddd, J = 7.6, 1H), 7.62 (td, J = 7.6, 1H),
7.35-7.43 (6H, m), 4.64 (2H, s), 3.82 (2H, s), 1.29 (6H, s); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) (δ ppm); 28.6, 46.3, 68.1, 78.9, 127.1, 127.7, 128.5, 129.4,
130.2, 137.2, 140.2, 164.9. MS (m/z): 300 [M+ + 1]. Anal. calcd. for
C18H18ClNO: C, 72.11; H, 6.05; Cl, 11.83; N, 4.67; O, 5.34. Found: C,
72.21; H, 6.10; N, 4.68.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New and Improved Synthesis of Telmisartan: An Antihypertensive Drug
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
