$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of CH(OH)(NC5H4)(C6H5) with SOCl2. An excess of SOCl2 (1 mL) was
added to a CH2Cl2 solution (3 mL) of (2-pyridyl)phenylmethanol (100 mg,
0.540 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at reflux conditions for 16
hours. The reaction mixture was then poured onto a cold saturated aqueous
solution of K2CO3 (20 mL). The aqueous phase was then extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3 x 20 mL) and the combined organic phases were dried over MgSO4
and filtered. Chromatographic separation on silica gel (eluent:
cyclohexane/ethylacetate 4:1, Rf = 0.5) of the residue obtained upon
evaporation of the filtered solution afforded pure
(2-pyridyl)phenylmethyl chloride as a yellow oil (109 mg, 0.535 mmol,
99%). (2-pyridyl)phenylmethyl chloride, Yield 109 mg, 0.535 mmol, 99% 1H
NMR (CDCl3): 8.58 (ddd, J(H,H) = 4.8, 1.8, 1.2, 1H, NC5H4), 7.70 (td,
J(H,H) = 8.0, 1.6, 1H, NC5H4), 7.58-7.27 (m, 6H, C6H5 and NC5H4), 7.19
(ddd, J(H,H) = 7.4, 4.8, 1.2, 1H, NC5H4), 6.19 (s, 1H, CHCl).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
