$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (-)-(1S,2S)-2-Chloro-1-phenyl-[2-D1]ethyl
benzoate {(1S,2S)-[2-D1]11}:4 A solution of
(1S,2R)-2-hydroxy-1-phenyl[2-D1]ethyl benzoate (190 mg, 0.78 mmol) and
Ph3P (307 mg, 1.17 mmol) in dry CH3CN/CCl4 (1.8 mL/0.75 mL) was stirred
for 2 h at RT under argon. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure
and the residue purified by flash chromatography [hexanes/EtOAc (20:1),
Rf = 0.44] to give benzoate (1S,2S)-[2-D1]11 (194 mg, 95%) as a colorless
oil. Similarly, (1R,2R)-2-hydroxy-1-phenyl-[2-D1]ethyl benzoate (210 mg,
0.86 mmol) was converted to (+)-(1R,2S)-2-chloro-1-phenyl-[2-D1]ethyl
benzoate {(1R,2S)-[2-D1]11} (222 mg, 99%). [α]20 D +35.8 (c 1.23,
acetone). IR (Si): 3034, 1722, 1451, 1315, 1267, 1110, 1070, 1026 cm-1.
1H NMR (400.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.14-8.09 (m, 2H), 7.60-7.55 (m, 1H),
7.49-7.31 (m, 7H), 6.19 (d, J = 4.4 Hz, 1H), 3.85 (br.d, J = 4.4 Hz, 1H).
13C NMR (100.61 MHz, CDCl3): δ 165.5, 137.2, 133.3, 129.8 (2C), 128.8,
128.7 (2C), 128.4 (2C), 126.6 (2C), 75.5, 46.4 (t, J = 23.3 Hz, 1C).
