$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure: To a stirring solution of
alcohol in 0.75-1.3 mL of freshly distilled CH2Cl2 (or CH3CN) was added
the dichlorocyclopropene. The mixture was stirred at 23 °C (or 80 °C) for
3 to 65 min, depending on the alcohol. When the reaction was complete
(monitored by TLC), the reaction mixture was eluted through a short
silica gel plug eluting with 10% EtOAc:hexanes. When necessary, the crude
chloride was purified by silica gel chromatography.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aromatic cation activation of alcohols: conversion to alkyl chlorides
using dichlorodiphenylcyclopropene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kelly, Brendan D.; Lambert, Tristan H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
