$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Chlorination Procedure for Allylic Alcohols: Potassium hydride
(30 % dispersion in mineral oil 1.2 equiv) was washed with hexane (3 mL)
and then a dioxane solution of the allylic alcohol (1 equiv) was added
dropwise. After 5 minutes solid NbCl5 (1.2 equiv) was added as a dry
powder. After 10 min1 the reaction mixture was poured into 2 M HCl and
then extracted with ethyl acetate. (E)-3-Napthyl-1-propenyl chloride
(2a). The general procedure was employed with 1- napthyl propenol2 (30
mg, 0.163 mmol), potassium hydride (26 mg, 0.196 mmol), niobium
pentachloride (53 mg, 0.196 mmol) and dioxane (1 mL) to afford 32 mg
(98%) of 3-napthyl-1- propenyl chloride (2a) 3 as an oil. oil: IR (film)
3048, 1594, 773 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.38 (d, J= 6.8 Hz, 2H),
6.39 (td, J= 15.2, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.58-7.42 (m, 4H), 7.64 (d, J= 6.8 Hz,
1H), 7.84 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.89 (d, J= 9.2 Hz, 1H), 8.12 (d, J= 7.6
Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 45.6, 123.6, 124.3, 125.6, 126.0,
126.3, 128.1, 128.6, 131.1, 131.3, 133.6; HRMS(ESI) calcd for (M+Na+),
C13H11ClNa+ 225.0455, found 225.0447.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Allylic and Allenic Halide Synthesis via NbCl5- and NbBr5-Mediated
Alkoxide Rearrangements
