$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (1-Chloromethyl-2-methylpropyl)-carbamic acid
benzyl ester: 2,4,6-Trichloro-[1,3,5]-triazine (1.83 g, 10.0 mmol) was
added to DMF (2 mL), maintained at 25 °C. After the formation of a white
solid, the reaction was monitored (TLC) until complete disappearance of
TCT, CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was added, followed by the alcohol (2.59 g, 9.5
mmol). After the addition, the mixture was stirred at room temperature,
monitored (TLC) until completion (4 h). Water (20 mL) was added then the
organic phase washed with 15 mL of a saturated solution of Na2CO3,
followed by 1 N HCl and brine. The organic layer were dried (Na2SO4) and
the solvent evaporated. (1-Chloromethyl-2-phenyl-ethyl)-carbamic acid
9H-fluoren-9-yl ester: (4 h, 3.47 g, 97%). [α]20 D -20.94 (c 0.4, CHCl3),
1H NMR δ 7.76 (d, 2H), 7.54 (t, 2H), 7.40 (t, 2H), 7.31 (m, 5H9, 7.17 (t,
2H); 13C NMR δ 159.2, 141.6, 138.6, 73.4, 54.7, 49.8, 38.9. Anal. Calcd.
for C23H20ClNO2 (377.86): C, 73.11; H, 5.33; Cl, 9.38 N, 3.71. Found C,
73.08, H, 5.33, Cl, 9.42, N, 3.71.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Route to Alkyl Chlorides from Alcohols Using the Complex
TCT/DMF
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM De Luca, Lidia; Giacomelli, Giampaolo; Porcheddu, Andrea
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(4), 553-555

