$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Benzyl Chlorides 4 from Alcohols 3; General
Procedure B: Ph3P (3 equiv) and CH2Cl2 (2 mL per 3.0 mmol Ph3P) were
added to a flask equipped with a magnetic stir bar. CBrCl3 (1.2 equiv)
was added, the flask was closed with a septum, and the mixture was
stirred under air at r.t. for 40 min, during which the colorless soln
turned deep brown. A soln of the requisite alcohol 3 (1.0 equiv) in
CH2Cl2 (3 mL per 1.0 mmol alcohol) was added dropwise, and the mixture
was stirred at r.t. until the starting material had been consumed (as
indicated by TLC; approximately 10 min). The mixture was diluted with a
Et2O-pentane mixture (3:1) until solid Ph3PO began to precipitate. The
heterogeneous mixture was then filtered through a pad of silica gel,
which was rinsed with a Et2O-pentane mixture (3:1). Rotary evaporation
provided clean 4 after most reactions, as indicated by 1H NMR
spectroscopy. The products were purified additionally by flash
chromatography. The product was purified by flash column chromatography
(silica gel, pentane); this provided 4a.
1-(Chloromethyl)-3,5-dinitrobenzene (4d): General procedure B was
followed (1 mmol scale). The product was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica gel, Et2O-pentane, 15:85); this provided 4d as a
white solid, yield 208 mg, 96%. mp 79-80°C (Lit.16 79-79.5°C). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.03 (t, J = 2.0 Hz, 1 H), 8.62 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 2
H), 4.76 (s, 2 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 148.7, 141.6, 128.6,
118.7, 43.5.
