$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Chlorination of 5-(2-hydroxyethyl)-4-methylthiazole (II) with phosphorus
pentaehloride (optimum procedure). To a suspension of 250.0 g (1.20 mole)
PC15 in 600 ml of anhydrous dichloroethane was added with stirring a
solution of 448.54 g (2.51 mole) of technical-grade II in 600 ml of
anhydrous dichloroethane, with the reaction mixture temperature
maintained within 5 - 7 °C When all dichloroethane solution of II was
introduced, the reaction mixture was heated on an oil bath to boiling and
boiled for 3 h. Then 600 ml of water was added with cooling, and the
mixture was stirred for 15- 20 min and neutralized with a concentrated
aqueous ammonia solution to pH 7- 8. The organic layer was separated, the
solvent was separated in vacuum, and the residue was distilled in vacuum
to obtain 96.1% 5-(2-ehloroethyl)-4-methylthiazole (I). Yield 400.3 g,
95%. b.p., 90 - 96°C (4 Torr); nD20 1.5463.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reagent gave lower yields
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 5-(2-chloroethyl)-4-methylthiazole using the reaction of
5-(2-hydroxyethyl)-4-methylthiazole with phosphorus pentachloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Antonov, E. A.; Zhirov, A. A.; Kirsanov, A. T.; Krivolapov, Yu. A.;
Sorokin, A. A.; Markovich, Yu. D.; Panfilov, A. V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Pharmaceutical Chemistry Journal (Translation of
Khimiko-Farmatsevticheskii Zhurnal) (2000), 33(12), 658-660

