$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Chloromethyl-pyrrolidine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester:
2,4,6-Trichloro-[1,3,5]-triazine (1.83 g, 10.0 mmol) was added to DMF (2
mL), maintained at 25 °C. After the formation of a white solid, CH2Cl2
(25 mL) was added, followed by NaHCO3 (3.19 g, 38.0 mmol) and
successively by N-Boc-prolinol (1.91 g, 9.5 mmol). After the addition,
the mixture was stirred at room temperature, monitored (TLC) until
completion (40 min). Water (20 mL) was added then the organic phase
washed with 15 mL of a saturated solution of Na2CO3, followed by 1 N HCl
and brine. The organic layer were dried (Na2SO4) and the solvent
evaporated. Pure 2-chloromethyl-pyrrolidine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl
ester (1.96 g, 94%). [α]20 D -7.78 (c 3.7, CHCl3), 1H NMR δ 3.92 (m, 1H),
3.57 (m, 2H) 3.34 (m, 2H), 1.94 (m, 2H), 1.79 (m, 2H), 1.43 (s, 9H); 13C
NMR δ 163.4, 66.9, 63.8, 59.7, 47.3, 36.3, 28.2, 23.5 Anal. Calcd. for
C10H18ClNO2 (219.71): C, 54.67; H, 8.26; Cl, 16.14; N, 6.38. Found C,
54.09, H, 8.26, Cl, 16.14, N, 6.36.
