$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Bromo-4-(3-methoxyphenyl)butane (22) To a stirring solution of 21
(5.43g, 30.1mmol) and carbon tetrabromide (12.5g, 37.7mmol) in
CH2Cl2(100mL) cooled to 0 °C under N2 atmosphere, triphenylphosphine
(11.9g, 45.2mmol) dissolved in CH2Cl2 (50mL) was added dropwise over
25min. After stirring for 1hr at 0 °C, the solution was warmed to room
temperature. After stirring for additional 12hr, the so)vent was
evaporated by rotary evaporation. Diethyl ether was added to the reaction
mixture to precipitate triphenylphosphine oxide and the resulting white
precipitates were filtered. Concentration in vacuo provided the crude
product as a yellow oil. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (80:20 petroleum ether:EtOAc) to give 22 as a colorless
oil (6.92g, 28.5mmol, 94%). 1-Bromo-4-(3-methoxyphenyl)butane (22), yield
6.92g, 28.5mmol, 94% 1H NMR(CDCl3, 400MHz) 6 1.75-1.83(m, 2H, ArCH2CH2-),
1.87-1.94(m, 2H, -CH2CH2Br), 2.64(t, J=7.6Hz, 2H, ArCH2-), 3.43(t,
J=7.2Hz, 2H, -CH2Br), 3.82(s, 3H, -OCH3), 6.75-6.78(m, 2H, Ar-H),
6.78-6.80(m, 1H, Ar-H), 7.20-7.24(m, 1H, Ar-H). 13C NMR(CDCl3, 100MHz) δ
29.62, 32.13, 33.60, 34.91, 55.04, 111.00, 114.12, 120.72, 129.25,
143.34, 159.57. HRMS-EI (M+) Calcd for C11H15BrO: 242.0306 Found:
242.0309.
