$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (5,5-dimethylhydantoinyl)-3-ethyl dimethylamine (DHEDA).
DHEDA was synthesized according to a reported method. In a 250 mL flask
in the ice bath, 12.83 g (0.11 mol) of 99 % thionyl chloride was added
and then 8.91 g (0.10 mol) of N,N-dimethyl ethanolamine was added
dropwise under stirring. The reaction mixture was heated to 35-50 °C
while being stirred for 1 h, and then, 150 mL of ethanol was added and
heated to its boiling. After cooling to room temperature, the
intermediate compound 2-dimethylaminoethyl chloride hydrochloride was
collected by filtration. After removal of the solvent by vacuum rotary
evaporation, a second crop was collected. 2-dimethylaminoethyl chloride
hydrochloride, yield of 91-94 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
