$DATUM Tris-1-adamantanylmethyl Chloride Tris-1-adamantanyl methanol (100 mg;
0.23 mmol) is added to a stirred solution of freshly distilled oxalyl
chloride (0.64 g, 5 mmol) in dry benzene (5 ml) at room temperature.
After standing overnight at room temperature removal excess oxalyl
chloride gives the crude chloride which is recrystallized from benzene.
Yield 97 mg, 93%. M.p. 227°C. 1H-NMR (200 MHz, C6D6/TMS): δ = 1.58 ppm
(45 H s). 13C-NMR (C6D6/TMS): δ = 30.2, 31.2, 38.3. 39.4, 53.3 ppm. MS
(70 eV): m/e = 416 (M - HCl), 135, 93, 79; C31H45Cl(453.1) calc. C 82.17
H 10.01 Cl 7.82, found C 82.12 H 9.89 Cl 7.35.
