$DATUM (chloromethyl)tributylstannane (2) and
(chloro-[D1]methyl)tributylstannane {[D1]2} - General Procedure B:4 To a
solution of tributylstannylmethanol (1) (200 mg, 0.62 mmol) and Ph3P (236
mg, 0.9 mmol) in dry CH3CN (1.2 mL) was added CCl4 (0.4 mL) under argon
atmosphere. The mixture was stirred for 1 h at RT, before the solvent was
removed under reduced pressure and the crude product purified by flash
chromatography [hexanes; Rf = 0.69] to yield chloromethylstannane 2 (196
mg, 93%) as a colorless oil. (chloromethyl)tributylstannane (2), yield
(196 mg, 93%) IR (Si): 2957, 2928, 2872, 2854, 1465, 1073 cm-1. 1H NMR
(400.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.04 (s, J(117/119Sn) = 16.2 Hz, 2H), 1.56-1.47
(m, J(117/119Sn) = 13.2 Hz, 6H), 1.30 (sext, J = 7.3 Hz, 6H), 1.00-0.95
(J(117/119Sn) = 52.2, 50.2 Hz, m, 6H), 0.88 (t, J = 7.3 Hz). 13C NMR
(100.61 MHz, CDCl3): δ 28.9 (J(117/119Sn) = 21.4 Hz, 3C), 27.3
(J(117/119Sn) = 55.8 Hz, 3C), 24.4, 13.7 (3C), 9.5 (J(117/119Sn) = 338.8,
325.5 Hz, 3C).
