$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Chloromethyl-3,5-dimethyl-4-nitropyridinehydrochloride (4) To a
solution of 2-hydroxymethyl-3,5-trimethyl-4-nitropyridine 3 (20 g, 0.11
mol) in CHCl3 (100 mL) at room temperature. SOCl2 (25 mL, 0.33 mol) was
slowly added. The mixture was allowed to heat to 50°C and stirred for 2
h. then excess SOCl2 and solvent were removed in vacuo. The residue was
dissolved in hoi ling toluene (100 mL), then cooled to 0°C, filtered,
washed with toluene (10 mL), and dried to give 4 (24.8 g) as a white
solid. Yield: 92.9%.
2-Chloromethyl-3,5-dimethyl-4-nitropyridinehydrochloride (4), yield (24.8
g, 92.9%). mp 125 - 126°C. 1H NMR (DMSO): 2.28 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.32 (s, 3H,
CH3). 4.94 (s, 2H, CH2). 8.60 (s, 1H, CH).
