$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for InCl3-Mediated Reactions
of Homoallyl Alcohols 1 with TMOF (2) InCl3 (3 mmol) was added to a
stirred solution of homoallyl alcohol 1 (3 mmol) and TMOF (2, 3 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (25 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at r.t. under Ar until 1
had been completely consumed (TLC). Then H2O (25 mL) was added and the
resulting mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (75 mL). The extracts were
washed with brine (25 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in
vacuo. The products were purified by Kugelrohr distillation or flash
chromatography on silica gel. The reaction with TiCl4 provided an
unexpected result, namely the exclusive formation of the homoallyl
chloride 5a in 92% yield (Table 2, entry 4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unexpected Lewis acid mediated reactions of 1-arylbut-3-en-1-ols with
trimethyl orthoformate - A new synthesis of homoallyl ethers and
chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Merisor, Elena; Conrad, Juergen; Malakar, Chandi C.; Beifuss, Uwe
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2008), (6), 903-907

