$DATUM Preparation of 2 from 1 with DMF as Solvent; Typical Procedure: A
solution of 1 (10 g, 79.4 mmol) in DMF (90 mL) was stirred at 25°Cand
POCl3 (12 g, 87.3 mmol) in DMF (10 mL) was added over 90 min via a
dropping funnel. After 6 h, the resulting mixture was analyzed for 2
(10.32 g, 90%), diluted with 1,1,1-trichloroethane (100 mL), stirred with
solid K2CO3 (22 g, 160 mmol) and allowed to stand for 1 h. The liquid
phase was discarded, the remaining solid suspended in
1,1,1-trichloroethane (100 mL) and hydrolyzed with crushed-ice (100 g).
The combined extracts were analysed for 2 (10.01 g, 97 % of the initial),
washed with H2O (5 x 50 mL) to extract DMF, analyzed for 2 (9.81 g, 95%
of the inital), dried (Na2SO4), filtered and the solvent removed (40-45
°C) at reduced pressure to yield crude 2 containing traces of DMF as the
main impurity (1H NMR). Oil, yield 10.5g, 92%. 1H NMR (CDCl3/TMS): δ =
9.57 (s, 1 H, CHO), 7.13 (d, 1 H, J = 3.6 Hz, H-3), 6.60 (d, 1 H, J = 3.6
Hz, H-4), 4.52 (s, 2 H, CH2).
