$DATUM 2-Chloro-1,2-diphenylethanone (3n)[5]Method A: 1,2-diphenylethanol (99
mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and TEMPO (8 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.1 equiv) were
dissolved in DCM (5 mL). TCCA (116 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was then
added in small portions. After stirring for 10 min at rt, MeOH (32 mg,
1.0 mmol, 2.0 equiv) was added dropwise. The reaction was stirred at rt
for 2 h and then concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude reaction
mixture was directly purified by FC on silica gel (pentane/Et2O 30:1).
The title compound was isolated. Colorless oil, yield (105 mg, 91%). 1H
NMR(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.07-7.91 (m, 2H, Ar-H), 7.61 - 7.28 (m, 8H, Ar-H),
6.35 (s, 1H, CHCl); 13C NMR(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 191.55 (CO), 135.95 (Ar-C),
134.35 (Ar- C), 133.80 (Ar-C), 129.25 (Ar-C), 129.21 (Ar-C), 129.18
(Ar-C), 128.85 (Ar-C), 128.54 (Ar- C), 62.33 (CHCl).
