$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Chloro-5-deoxy-1,2-O-isopropylidene-α-D-glucurono-6,3-lactone (8). A
solution of sulfuryl chloride (10 μL, 0.14 mmol) in DMF (200 μL) was
added drop-wise to a solution of the alcohol 4 (20 mg, 0.10 mmol) and
imidazole (31 mg, 0.46 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) at -40°C. The reaction mixture
was then warmed to rt and stirred for 1 h. The reaction mixture was
diluted with water (10 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 5 mL). The
combined organic extracts were dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated
in vacuo. Flash chromatography (1:1 EtOAc/hexane) of the residue gave the
chloride 8. A small portion was recrystallized from EtOAc/hexane. Yield:
21 mg, 91%, solid, colorless crystals. m.p. 92-98°C; [α]D +62.7 (c 0.9,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 Mhz, CDCl3): δ 6.00 (d, 1H, J1,2= 3.5 Hz, H-1), 4.99
(dd, 1H, J4,5= 4.4 Hz, J3,4= 2.6, H-4), 4.85 (d, 1H, J1,2= 3.5 Hz, H-2),
4.84 (d, 1H, J3,4= 2.6 Hz, H-3), 4.59 (d, 1H, J4,5= 4.4 Hz, H-5), 1.51
(s, 3H, CH3), 1.33 (s, 3H, CH3); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 169.4 (C-6),
113.6 (C(CH3)2), 106.6 (C-1), 82.7, 82.6, (C-2,-3), 78.5 (C-4), 54.6
(C-5), 26.9, 26.5 (C(CH3)2). HR ESMS m/z 257.0203 (M+Na+, calcd for
C9H11ClNaO5 257.0187).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
