$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General protocol: To a stirred solution of the primary alcohol (0.2 mmol)
in dichloromethane (0.4 mL, 0.5 M) at room temperature under argon was
added successively the tetraethylammonium halide (0.3 mmol) and
2,6-lutidine (69 μL, 0.6 mmol). XtalFluor-E (69 mg, 0.3 mmol) was then
added and the solution was stirred for 18 h at the same temperature. The
reaction mixture was quenched by aqueous sodium carbonate (5%) and the
aqueous phase was extracted with dichloromethane (3X). The combined
organic extracts were washed with 10% HCl (1X), water (1X) and brine
(1X). Then, the resulting mixture was dried over anhydrous MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was purified with
flash chromatography to give the desired product. 5-Bromopentylbenzene
(2a). Following the general protocol on a 0.31 mmol scale of
5-phenylpentanol (1a) using tetraethylammonium bromide, the desired
product (63 mg, 91%) was isolated as clear oil by flash chromatography
using 100% hexanes.The same reaction performed on a 6.46 mmol scale gave
73% isolated yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33-7.23 (m, 2H),
7.22-7.11 (m, 3H), 3.55-3.49 (m, 2H), 2.62 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 1.85-1.74
(m, 2H), 1.70-1.59 (m, 2H), 1.55-1.41 (m, 2H). Spectral data for 2a were
identical with those previously reported.11
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on source of bromine, solvent and concentration, optimization
study, scalable (gram scale)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of Primary Alcohols Using a Tetraethylammonium
Halide/[Et2NSF2]BF4 Combination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pouliot, Marie-France; Mahe, Olivier; Hamel, Jean-Denys; Desroches,
Justine; Paquin, Jean-Francois
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(21), 5428-5431

