$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3,7-Bis(chloromethyl)-5H-dibenzo[b,d]thiophene-5,5-dione (IV). A mixture
of 3,7-bis-(hydroxymethyl)-dibenzothiophene-5,5-dione I (2.76 g, 1.0
mmol), 10 ml of toluene, and 0.5 ml (∼7 mmol, 3.5 eq.) of thionyl
chloride were refluxed till HCl stopped releasing. The solvent was
evacuated with the rotor evaporator; the residue was dissolved in 50 ml
of hexane and purified by flash-chromatography. Yield 1.97 g (91%),
colorless crystals. mp 159.0-161.5°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3063, 3043,
3020, 2977, 2940, 2873, 1463, 1447, 1420, 1400, 1327, 1310, 1290, 1273,
1260, 1257, 1213, 1160, 1150, 1090, 1077, 933, 900, 880, 827, 820, 733,
727, 710, 703, 680. Found, %: C 53.65; H 3.20. C14H10Cl2O2S. Calculated,
%: C 53.68; H 3.22. M 313.21. 1H NMR, (DMSO-d6), δ, ppm
5,5-dioxodibenzothiophene: 4.93 s (4H, CH2Cl), 7.59 d.d (2H, H2,8 Dbt,
Jortho 8.5, Jmeta 1.5 Hz,), 8.13 d (2H, H4,6 Dbt, Jmeta 1.5 Hz), 8.38 d
(2H, H1,9 Dbt, Jortho 8.5 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and fungicidal activity of the quaternary ammonium salts of the
1,3,7-substituted dibenzothiophene-5,5-diones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Vasilevskii, D. A.; Petushok, V. G.; Kalechits, G. V.; Zheldakova, R. A.;
Ol'khovik, V. K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2013), 83(9), 1698-1702

