$DATUM 603-35-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Dendritic Benzyl Chlorides 2 Triphenylphosphine was added to a mixture of
the dendritic benzyl alcohol 2-OH with appropriate amount solvent, and
the mixture was heated at reflux and stirred under nitrogen for 24 h. For
higher generation, a larger amount of triphenylphosphine was required.
After the reaction was completed, the reaction mixture was evaporated and
dried. The crude product was purified as outlined in the following text.
Compound 2c was prepared from 2c-OH (1.00 equiv) and triphenylphosphine
(2.50 equiv) in CCl4 and CH2Cl2 (v/v, 1:1). The residue was purified by
flash chromatography with petroleum ether (bp 60-90 °C)/CH2Cl2 (v/v, 1:2)
as the eluent to give 2c as a colorless glass: yield 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of dendritic phenol ether derivatives with a naphthalene core
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xiang, Zhonghua; Cao, Derong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2008), 38(9), 1318-1324

